scope: |
  The Corpus Contract nightly has been RED for eight nights (2026-08-07 .. 08-14). The entry blames
  a 08-13 reporting change; the per-night census refutes that — the streak is FOUR different failure
  sets, and the current five rows appeared on 08-10, three days earlier.

  ROOT CAUSE MEASURED, not inferred: `531a0e451` (08-09 17:43) moved the 108 shared `.ssc` std
  modules to the repo-root `std/`. SEVEN examples still import them by the pre-move relative path
  `../runtime/std/…`, so the interpreter answers `Import not found`, the case is SKIPped on every
  lane for `int-nonzero`, and a skipped case cannot produce the verdicts its baseline froze. All ten
  distinct import targets exist under `std/`; correcting one path and running it on int removes the
  error and exits 0. `0796774ad` explains the fifth row separately — it removed
  `native-import-in-fence js KNOWN-RED` from BOTH halves while the js defect persisted.

  Two of the seven, `remote-registry-rpc` and `streams`, do NOT appear as regressions because their
  `* SKIP` is FROZEN IN THE BASELINE — a baseline row enshrining a stale path. They are in scope for
  that reason: fixing the path makes a frozen known-red start passing, which fails the suite by
  design, so both halves move together.

  NARROW: seven example import paths, the baseline rows that freeze their skips, and the roster
  digest paired with the baseline. No compiler or harness change.
